Windows: the slim profile's build, without Dawn.

Chrome always has Dawn on Windows; the slim profile has none (patches/0013 did
the same for macOS). gpu_init.cc and the D3D backing factory named its context
provider without the build flag the other platforms have, as do, since 157,
gpu_init_win.cc and GpuInit2 (gpu_init_2.cc), which share its Windows code. And WebNN's ONNX
Runtime back end, which is Windows' alone, uses fp16 without depending on it,
so its include path is not there unless another back end brings it.

